---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const mug=core.products.find(p=>p.product_id==='P7')!;
---
<figure class="authority" aria-labelledby="r25-authority-title" data-authority>
<figcaption id="r25-authority-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Which identity decides the visible shop?</figcaption>
<div class="inputs"><label>Database login <select data-login aria-label="Database login"><option value="10">runtime_10</option><option value="20">runtime_20</option></select></label><label>Caller sets app.shop_id <select data-claimed aria-label="Caller sets app.shop_id"><option value="10">10</option><option value="20">20</option></select></label></div>
<fieldset><legend>The policy trusts</legend><label><input name="r25-rule" type="radio" value="setting" checked /> Caller setting</label><label><input name="r25-rule" type="radio" value="identity" /> Database identity</label></fieldset>
<div class="sql"><code>SELECT name, price FROM shop.products<br />WHERE product_id = 'P7';</code></div>
<div class="boundary"><p class="rule" data-rule>Policy: shop_id = caller setting (10)</p><table><caption>Two different products share the text P7</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Product</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">Query result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-shop="10"><td>(10, P7)</td><td>{mug.name}</td><td>{mug.price}</td><td data-verdict>Returned</td></tr><tr data-shop="20"><td>(20, P7)</td><td>Copper mug</td><td>18.00</td><td data-verdict>Hidden</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite">runtime_10 receives Blue mug, 20.00.</p>
<details><summary>What the comparison shows</summary><p>With the caller-setting rule, setting 10 returns Blue mug and setting 20 returns Copper mug, whichever database login is used. With the database-identity rule, runtime_10 returns Blue mug and runtime_20 returns Copper mug, whichever setting the caller supplies. This assumes neither runtime login can become the other or assume the owner’s authority.</p></details>
<p class="caption">An illustrative comparison of two policies, not a database running in the browser. “Hidden” means this SELECT returns no such row; it is not a claim that row security covers every privileged path or information channel.</p>
</figure>
<script>
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-authority]')){
 const select=(name:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>(name)!;
 const render=()=>{
  const login=select('[data-login]').value;
  const claimed=select('[data-claimed]').value;
  const identity=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked')!.value==='identity';
  const shop=identity?login:claimed;
  root.querySelector('[data-rule]')!.textContent=identity?`Policy: shop_id = shop for current_user (runtime_${login} → ${shop})`:`Policy: shop_id = caller setting (${shop})`;
  for(const row of root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-shop]')){
   const shown=row.dataset.shop===shop;
   row.dataset.shown=String(shown);
   row.querySelector('[data-verdict]')!.textContent=shown?'Returned':'Hidden';
  }
  const crossed=login!==shop;
  root.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=`runtime_${login} receives ${shop==='10'?'Blue mug, 20.00':'Copper mug, 18.00'}.${crossed?' The caller setting crossed the intended tenant boundary.':identity?' Changing the caller setting cannot select another shop.':' Change the caller setting to try the other shop.'}`;
 };
 root.querySelectorAll('input,select').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',render));render();
}
</script>
<style>
.authority{font:.95rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:2.2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:1rem}.authority figcaption{font:1.2rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}.authority figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}.inputs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem}.inputs label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;flex:1;min-width:12rem}select{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.5rem}fieldset{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;border:0;padding:0;margin:1rem 0}legend{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.5rem}fieldset label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;cursor:pointer}.sql{padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);font-size:.85rem}.boundary{margin-top:1rem;border:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.7rem}.rule{margin:0 0 .5rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.authority table{display:table;table-layout:fixed;font-size:.85rem;margin:0;width:100%}.authority caption{text-align:left;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-bottom:.5rem}.authority th,.authority td{padding:.5rem .3rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.authority tr[data-shown=true]{background:var(--color-surface-alt)}.authority [data-verdict]{font-weight:600}.result{border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem;min-height:3em}.caption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}summary{cursor:pointer}input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:500px){.authority{padding:.75rem}.boundary{padding:.35rem}.authority table{font-size:.75rem}.authority th,.authority td{padding:.4rem .2rem}.inputs label{min-width:0;flex-basis:100%}.sql code{font-size:.75rem}.result{min-height:6em}}
</style>
